R10 green (10 pass). Next: R11 — conflito de sala.

R11: encontros de atividades não canceladas na mesma sala precisam de mínimo 15 min entre fim de um e início do próximo (10h14 conflita; 10h15 ok). Violação → 409 CONFLITO_DE_SALA. Atividades canceladas não bloqueiam.

I need to seed an existing activity in the same sala, then try to POST a new one with a conflicting/ok encontro.

Seeding: I'll add a helper semearAtividade to the spec file (like the m1-grade.spec.js). Copy from there.

Test plan:
- Seed existing: laje (lab-3) activity "Palestra ocupada" with encontro { inicio: 2026-10-19T19:00:00-03:00, fim: 2026-10-19T20:00:00-03:00 }.
- POST new activity in lab-3 with encontro at 20:00:00-03:00 (exactly 20:00 → 0 min gap) → conflict. Better: the spec example: fim at 10:00, next starts 10:14 → conflita; 10:15 ok. In our case existing fim 20:00, new inicio 20:14 → 14 min gap → 409 CONFLITO_DE_SALA; new inicio 20:15 → ok 201.

So:
- new encontro starts 2026-10-19T20:14:00-03:00 → 409 CONFLITO_DE_SALA
- new encontro starts 2026-10-19T20:15:00-03:00 → 201
- Also test canceled activity doesn't block: seed a canceled activity in lab-3 with encontro that would conflict, POST should still 201.

The new activity is minicurso with 2 encontros — I need the non-conflicting second encontro on another day. And the conflicting first encontro on 19/10 20:14. Use segundoValido on 21/10.

Wait, careful: new atividade minicurso needs 2 encontros. Both checked against existing. First 19/10 20:14 (conflict with existing 19/10 19-20). Second 21/10 (no conflict). → 409.

For the "15 min ok" case: first encontro 19/10 20:15, second 21/10 → 201.

For canceled: seed canceled activity in lab-3 with encontro 19/10 20:00-21:00 say; new activity with encontro 19/10 21:00 (0 gap → would conflict if not canceled) → 201.

Also should check the reverse direction (existing after new)? The criteria only test one direction. I'll do one direction (new starts too soon after existing). But my implementation should handle both directions symmetric.

Also the conflict must be only same sala and only non-canceled. My implementation: query all non-canceled activities, their encontros, filter same sala, and check 15-min separation between each pair of (new encontro, existing encontro) — against all existing encontros of non-canceled activities in the same sala.

Implementation:

```js
function temConflitoDeSala(salaId, encontros) {
  const atividadesNaSala = banco.prepare('SELECT id, cancelada FROM atividades WHERE salaId = ?').all(salaId);
  for (const atv of atividadesNaSala) {
    if (atv.cancelada) continue;
    const existentes = encontrosPorAtividade.all(atv.id);
    for (const existente of existentes) {
      for (const novo of encontros) {
        const inicioNovoMs = Date.parse(novo.inicio);
        const fimNovoMs = Date.parse(novo.fim);
        const inicioExMs = Date.parse(existente.inicio);
        const fimExMs = Date.parse(existente.fim);
        const folga = 15 * 60000;
        const semConflito = fimExMs + folga <= inicioNovoMs || fimNovoMs + folga <= inicioExMs;
        if (!semConflito) return true;
      }
    }
  }
  return false;
}
```

Wait — the "no conflict" condition: two encontros are fine if there are at least 15 min between them. i.e., either new starts >= 15 min after existing ends, or existing starts >= 15 min after new ends. `fimExMs + folga <= inicioNovoMs` = existing ends, +15min, new starts. `fimNovoMs + folga <= inicioExMs` = new ends,+15min, existing starts. If neither → conflict (overlap or too-close). Good.

Where to call in route: after VAGAS_ACIMA_DA_CAPACIDADE (R12 order: quantity → encontro → vagas → conflito). Add:

```js
if (temConflitoDeSala(salaId, corpo.encontros)) {
  return res.status(409).json({ erro: 'CONFLITO_DE_SALA', mensagem: 'A sala já tem atividade cobrindo esse horário com menos de 15 min de folga.' });
}
```

Let me write the test first.

